---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/usgaap/asc852.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — Chapter 11 Reorganizations" },
        { id: "s3", label: "The Two-Part Fresh-Start Eligibility Test" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Fresh-Start Reporting Mechanics — Revaluation to Fair Value" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Reorganization Value and Its Allocation" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Financial Statement Presentation — Predecessor vs Successor" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — the Fresh-Start Eligibility Test" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Fresh-Start Balance Sheet Adjustment" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "No Direct IFRS Equivalent — Discussion" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Topics" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A genuinely new reporting entity emerges from bankruptcy</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">When a company emerges from Chapter 11 bankruptcy reorganization having genuinely SHED most of its old liabilities and OWNERSHIP has substantially changed hands, ASC 852 treats the emerging entity — under specific conditions — as effectively a NEW reporting entity: assets and liabilities are RESTATED to FAIR VALUE (much like a business combination), and the ACCUMULATED DEFICIT is RESET to zero. This "FRESH-START REPORTING" mechanism gives financial statement users a clean, forward-looking starting point, rather than carrying forward historical costs and an accumulated deficit built up under a capital structure that no longer exists.</div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Chapter 11 Reorganizations</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A genuinely US-specific legal context</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">ASC 852 applies to entities undergoing reorganization under CHAPTER 11 of the US BANKRUPTCY CODE — a specific US legal proceeding allowing a financially distressed entity to restructure its debts and operations while continuing as a going concern, typically under a court-confirmed PLAN of reorganization.</div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>The Two-Part Fresh-Start Eligibility Test</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">BOTH conditions must be met</div>
    <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.4fr 2.6fr;"><span>Test</span><span>Requirement</span></div>
    <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.4fr 2.6fr;"><span>1</span><span>The REORGANIZATION VALUE of the entity's assets IMMEDIATELY BEFORE confirmation of the plan is LESS THAN the total of post-petition liabilities and allowed claims — i.e. the entity was genuinely insolvent on a going-concern reorganization-value basis</span></div>
    <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.4fr 2.6fr;"><span>2</span><span>Holders of EXISTING VOTING SHARES immediately before plan confirmation receive LESS THAN 50% of the VOTING SHARES of the EMERGING entity — i.e. genuine, substantial change of CONTROL/OWNERSHIP has occurred</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="note">BOTH conditions must be satisfied for FRESH-START reporting to apply — if either condition fails (e.g. the old shareholders retain majority control of the emerged entity), the entity continues its PRE-EXISTING basis of accounting instead.</div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Fresh-Start Reporting Mechanics — Revaluation to Fair Value</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">A clean slate, valued as if newly created</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">When fresh-start reporting applies, the emerging entity's ASSETS and LIABILITIES are RESTATED to their FAIR VALUES as of the fresh-start reporting date, and the ACCUMULATED DEFICIT is RESET TO ZERO — the entity's financial statements essentially begin again, as if it were a genuinely NEW reporting entity, even though it is legally a continuation of the same company.</div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Reorganization Value and Its Allocation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Similar mechanics to a business combination purchase price allocation</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">The entity's total REORGANIZATION VALUE (broadly, its going-concern fair value immediately after restructuring) is ALLOCATED to individual assets and liabilities using an approach analogous to ASC 805's business combination purchase price allocation — identifiable assets and liabilities are recorded at their individual fair values, with any EXCESS reorganization value over identifiable net assets recognised similarly to GOODWILL.</div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Financial Statement Presentation — Predecessor vs Successor</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A "black-line" divider between two distinct reporting periods</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">Financial statements are presented with a clear BLACK-LINE division between the "PREDECESSOR" company (the entity's financial statements up to and including the fresh-start date) and the "SUCCESSOR" company (the entity's financial statements from the fresh-start date forward) — reflecting that these are, in a genuine accounting sense, TWO DIFFERENT REPORTING ENTITIES, even though they represent the same continuing legal enterprise and operations.</div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — the Fresh-Start Eligibility Test</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Applying both conditions</div>
    <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A manufacturer emerging from Chapter 11</div><div class="wk-body">A manufacturer's reorganization value immediately before plan confirmation is determined to be $80,000,000, while its post-petition liabilities and allowed claims total $120,000,000. Under the confirmed plan, former shareholders receive only 5% of the new voting shares, with creditors receiving the remaining 95% in exchange for their claims.</div><div class="wk-answer">Test 1: Reorganization value ($80,000,000) < total liabilities/claims ($120,000,000) → <strong>MET</strong>. Test 2: Former shareholders retain only 5% of voting shares, well under 50% → <strong>MET</strong>. Since BOTH conditions are satisfied, the entity <strong>QUALIFIES for fresh-start reporting</strong> upon emergence.</div></div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Fresh-Start Balance Sheet Adjustment</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Resetting the balance sheet</div>
    <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Restating assets and eliminating the accumulated deficit</div><div class="wk-body">Immediately before fresh-start, the entity's historical-cost net assets are $50,000,000, with an accumulated deficit of $200,000,000. Its fresh-start reorganization value, allocated to identifiable assets and liabilities at fair value, totals $80,000,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">Assets and liabilities are REVALUED to their individual fair values (aggregating to the $80,000,000 reorganization value, with any excess treated similarly to goodwill). The PRE-EXISTING $200,000,000 accumulated deficit is <strong>ELIMINATED (reset to zero)</strong> — the SUCCESSOR entity begins its life with a clean retained earnings balance of $0, even though the underlying operating business and workforce continue unchanged.</div></div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASC 852 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Reorganization items presented separately in the predecessor entity's income statement (e.g. professional fees, gains/losses on settlement of liabilities subject to compromise)</span><span>Condensed combined financial statements during the Chapter 11 proceeding, if practicable</span><span>Details of the fresh-start adjustments and the allocation of reorganization value upon emergence</span></div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
    <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether both fresh-start eligibility conditions are met, particularly the voting share retention threshold</span><span>Classifying items as reorganization-related versus ordinary operating activity during Chapter 11</span></div></div>
    <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Reorganization value of the entity as a going concern</span><span>Fair value of individual identifiable assets and liabilities for allocation purposes</span></div></div></div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>No Direct IFRS Equivalent — Discussion</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A genuinely US-specific Topic, tied to a specific national legal framework</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">IFRS does NOT have a DEDICATED standard equivalent to ASC 852's fresh-start reporting framework — there is no direct IAS/IFRS counterpart, since the concept is fundamentally tied to CHAPTER 11 of the US BANKRUPTCY CODE, a specific national legal proceeding without a precise structural analogue in most other jurisdictions' insolvency regimes. An IFRS reporter undergoing an analogous restructuring might, in rare circumstances, apply general IFRS principles (e.g. derecognition of extinguished liabilities, fair value remeasurement where otherwise required) to achieve SOME similar economic outcomes — but WITHOUT a single, dedicated, codified "fresh-start" framework paralleling ASC 852's specific two-part eligibility test and predecessor/successor presentation convention. This makes ASC 852 one of the narrower Topics in this library with genuinely NO direct standard-level IFRS counterpart, similar in that respect to ASC 808 (Collaborative Arrangements).</div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every ASC 852 event lands</div>
    <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
    <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Reorganization items during Chapter 11</span><span><span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Presented separately from ordinary operating results</span></div>
    <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Fresh-start adjustment</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge be">SE</span></span><span>Assets/liabilities revalued to fair value; accumulated deficit reset to zero</span></div>
    </div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Topics</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
    <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Topic</span><span>Connection</span></div>
    <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 805</span><span>Supplies the purchase-price-allocation-style mechanics used to allocate reorganization value to individual assets/liabilities</span></div>
    <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 820</span><span>Supplies the fair value measurement framework applied throughout fresh-start reporting</span></div>
    <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 470</span><span>Debt — governs extinguishment/modification accounting for liabilities settled or restructured during the Chapter 11 process</span></div>
    </div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cn span2">
    <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Fresh-start reporting</div><div class="glossary-def">A method of accounting in which an entity emerging from Chapter 11 restates its assets and liabilities to fair value and resets its accumulated deficit to zero, upon meeting specific eligibility conditions.</div></div>
    <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Reorganization value</div><div class="glossary-def">The fair value of an entity's assets immediately before plan confirmation, generally equivalent to the amount a willing buyer would pay for the reorganized entity's assets immediately after restructuring.</div></div>
    <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Predecessor / successor company</div><div class="glossary-def">The presentation convention distinguishing an entity's financial statements before (predecessor) and after (successor) the fresh-start reporting date.</div></div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asc852 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>

